  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "The study introduces the Congestion Propensity Index (CPI), a predictive metric calculated at the county level to evaluate expected congestion development across the United States. The index integrates traditional congestion drivers like population density, active transit modes, and spatial opportunity distribution with specific indicators of urbanization and suburbanization dynamics.",
      "why": "It provides a nationally comparable metric that captures variation within metropolitan areas rather than treating entire cities as homogeneous units, allowing planners to tailor transportation policies to specific suburban and urban contexts."
